# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.DS_Store
supabase/.DS_Store

# uploaded photos (served by the Go server)
uploads/
.claude/launch.json

# Vitest coverage output
coverage/

# GitNexus index: machine-local, rebuilt per machine
.gitnexus/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- JS deps ---
# Installed artefacts, never committed. `node_modules/` was committed by
# accident in cc6a258 and untracked again during the Phase 6 frontend work:
# one root `npm install` rebuilds every workspace, and tracking the result
# turns each install into thousands of lines of diff and a merge conflict
# inside somebody else's package.
#
# Unanchored (no leading slash) on purpose: this is an npm workspace, so a
# nested `node_modules/` under web-app/ or desktop-app/frontend/ is a mistake
# worth ignoring rather than committing -- see the note in scripts/dev.sh.
node_modules/
.npm/
jspm_packages/

# pnpm and yarn, in case either is ever used here instead of npm. Cheap to
# carry, and the cost of missing one is another 15,000-file commit.
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm/
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged
.yarn/build-state.yml
.yarn/install-state.gz
.pnp.*

# Package-manager logs
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npmrc.local

# Vite's on-disk caches, when they land outside node_modules
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Only ONE lockfile belongs in this repo. npm is what the scripts and CI run;
# a stray pnpm/yarn lock beside it means two tools disagree about the tree.
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock

# ------------------------------------------------------------- JS builds ---
# Vite output. desktop-app/frontend/dist keeps a tracked .gitkeep because
# desktop-app/main.go does `//go:embed all:frontend/dist`, and the directory
# has to exist on a fresh clone for `go build ./...` to work at all.
desktop-app/frontend/dist/*
!desktop-app/frontend/dist/.gitkeep
web-app/dist/

# Per-run service logs written by scripts/dev.sh and dev.ps1
.run-logs/

# Wails-generated JS bindings, regenerated by `wails dev` and `wails build`.
# Nothing in the repo imports them -- desktop-app/main.go embeds frontend/dist
# and nothing else -- and tracking them produced pure file-mode churn, flapping
# between 100755 and 100644 with no content change, on every regeneration.
# Verified by building with the directory absent: svelte-check, vite build and
# `go build ./...` all pass.
desktop-app/frontend/wailsjs/
